</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAfc" aria-labelledby="Sponsorships"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Sponsorships">Sponsorships</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Sage_Group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Sponsorships"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAfg"><a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Marussia_MR01_Sage_Newcastle_March_2012.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAfk"><img resource="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Marussia_MR01_Sage_Newcastle_March_2012.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Marussia_MR01_Sage_Newcastle_March_2012.jpg/250px-Marussia_MR01_Sage_Newcastle_March_2012.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4868" data-file-height="2640" data-file-type="bitmap" height="136" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Marussia_MR01_Sage_Newcastle_March_2012.jpg/500px-Marussia_MR01_Sage_Newcastle_March_2012.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAfo"/></a><figcaption id="mwAfs">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marussia_F1" title="Marussia F1" id="mwAfw">Marussia F1</a> promotional car on display in Sage's Newcastle headquarters.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAf0">The Sage Group was a patron of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sage_Gateshead" title="The Sage Gateshead" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAf4">The Sage Gateshead</a>, a Tyneside music venue designed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Foster,_Baron_Foster_of_Thames_Bank" title="Norman Foster, Baron Foster of Thames Bank" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAf8">Sir Norman Foster</a>. Now known as the Glasshouse Gateshead, it was completed in 2004 at a cost of £70 million, and has since become a main sight on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Tyne" title="River Tyne" id="mwAgA">River Tyne</a>. It is primarily used as a concert venue and centre for musical education, but also hosts other events including conferences.<sup about="#mwt173" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sponsor_14-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sponsor"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sponsor-14" id="mwAgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgM">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAgU">In 2008, Sage funded the revival of <i id="mwAgY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Krypton_Factor" title="The Krypton Factor" id="mwAgc">The Krypton Factor</a></i> television series for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITV_(TV_network)" title="ITV (TV network)" id="mwAgg">ITV</a> as a part of the Business Brain Training campaign.<sup about="#mwt176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgs">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgw">]</span></span></a></sup> Sage were the football shirt sponsor in May 2011 for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitley_Bay_F.C." title="Whitley Bay F.C." id="mwAg0">Whitley Bay F.C.</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FA_Vase" title="FA Vase" id="mwAg4">FA Vase</a> winning match.<sup about="#mwt179" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAg8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhE">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhI">]</span></span></a></sup> Sage had previously been a minor sponsor for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newcastle_United_F.C." title="Newcastle United F.C." id="mwAhM">Newcastle United F.C.</a><sup about="#mwt183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwAhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhY">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAhg">For the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012_Formula_One_season" title="2012 Formula One season" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhk">2012 Formula One season</a>, Sage were an official supplier for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marussia_F1" title="Marussia F1" id="mwAho">Marussia F1</a> team, and for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Formula_One_season" title="2013 Formula One season" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhs">2013</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Formula_One_season" title="2014 Formula One season" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhw">2014 seasons</a> Sage logos were placed on the car.<sup about="#mwt186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAh0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAh4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh8">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiA">]</span></span></a></sup> For the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017–18_Bristol_City_F.C._season" title="2017–18 Bristol City F.C. season" id="mwAiE">2017–18 Bristol City F.C. season</a>, Sage<!--via Sage Partner Percipient--> has partnered with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bristol_City_F.C." title="Bristol City F.C." id="mwAiI">Bristol City F.C.</a> as minor sponsor through its provision of Sage X3 for Bristol Sport.<!-- with the company logo appearing on the team shorts and background of interview pieces and news conferences --><sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAiM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiU">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-50" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-50" id="mwAic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAik">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAio">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAis">Sage sponsored the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invictus_Games" title="Invictus Games" id="mwAiw">Invictus Games</a> in a multi-year partnership starting in 2016.<sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAi0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAi4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAi8">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjA">]</span></span></a></sup> Sage also sponsored the 2019 editions of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reading_Half_Marathon" title="Reading Half Marathon" id="mwAjE">Reading Half Marathon</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blaydon_Race" title="Blaydon Race" id="mwAjI">Blaydon Race</a>.<sup about="#mwt198" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-52" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-52" id="mwAjM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjU">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt201" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-53" id="mwAjc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjk">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjo">]</span></span></a></sup> Sage are an official partner of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hundred_(cricket)" title="The Hundred (cricket)" id="mwAjs">The Hundred</a> cricket tournament.<sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwAjw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAj0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj4">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj8">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025 Sage became the Official Finance Software Partner of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LPGA" title="LPGA" id="mwAkA">LPGA</a> in a multi-year deal.<sup about="#mwt207" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwAkE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkM">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAkU">Sage are sponsoring the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Rugby_World_Cup" title="2023 Rugby World Cup" id="mwAkY">2023 Rugby World Cup</a>,<sup about="#mwt210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAkc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkk">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAko">]</span></span></a></sup> as well as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Six_Nations_Championship" title="Six Nations Championship" id="mwAks">Six Nations Championship</a>.<sup about="#mwt213" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwAkw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAk0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk4">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk8">]</span></span></a></sup> Starting in the 2023 season Sage are an official partner of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_League_Baseball" title="Major League Baseball" id="mwAlA">Major League Baseball</a>.<sup about="#mwt216" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwAlE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlM">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Additionally, opening 2025, Sage are the named sponsor of the new <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newcastle_upon_Tyne" title="Newcastle upon Tyne" id="mwAlU">Newcastle</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateshead" title="Gateshead" id="mwAlY">Gateshead</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quayside" title="Quayside" id="mwAlc">Quayside</a> arena and conference centre, named "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sage" title="The Sage" id="mwAlg">The Sage</a>".<sup about="#mwt219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAlk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAls">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

